# ─── Secrets — NEVER commit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These were git-tracked with REAL prod keys and history-purged 2026-07-23.
# The keys they held are being ROTATED; keep any local copies OUT of git.
ENCRYPTION_KEYS.txt
ENCRYPTION_KEYS*.txt
ROTATED_SECRETS*.txt
deploy.sh
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
server/.env
client/.env
# …but keep the placeholder templates in version control:
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ─── Dependencies / build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# …EXCEPT the two builds we deploy. The production box has ~560MB free and runs
# five other apps, so it never builds — `client/dist` and `server/dist` ship in
# git and nginx/pm2 serve them straight from the working tree.
#
# They were force-added once and then left ignored, which is a trap that nearly
# broke a deploy: a rebuild renames every hashed asset, so `git add` staged the
# MODIFIED `index.html` (pointing at `index-<new>.js`) and the 55 DELETED old
# assets while silently skipping all 56 new ones — leaving an index that asks
# for a bundle no longer in the repo. A blank site, from a commit that looked
# fine. Un-ignoring them makes `git status` tell the truth instead.
!client/dist/
!client/dist/**
!server/dist/
!server/dist/**

# ─── Test / tooling artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
client/test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright/

# ─── Logs / OS cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
